00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.530 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this animation shows how China's leader  Xi Jinping Consolidated power within the  Communist Party by stacking it with  loyalists and how he broke some key  long-standing party rules in order to do  so it's based on a Bloomberg News  analysis of appointments of the  Communist Party Central Committee since  1992 some  1300 appointments so far the Communist  party's leadership is made up of more  than 300 officials divided in a  five-level hierarchy at the top of  course is the General Secretary of Xi  Jinping who also serves as the president  and commander-in-chief of the Communist  party's military  below him is the Supreme seven-man  standing committee the 25-member top  decision-making pilot Bureau and then  the much larger Central Committee and  his alternates each Congress provides  the opportunity to rejig the ranks while  China has denied having a retirement age  for top Communist Party officials no one  has breached 68 in the upper ranks of  power for decades but now at 69 she is  expected to secure a precedentifying  third term going past that age cap  two other members of the current signing  committee are also due to age out under  that rule whether she breaks that Norm  just for himself or for the other two as  well remains to be seen  [Music]

